1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Most AI ends curiosity
with an answer.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
ReasonWeave makes learner
thinking visible.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is a clearly labeled,
pre-generated journey.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
It is reliable, not a
live model call.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Learners choose a method,
then build.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
No account, profile,
or gradebook is needed.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Three methods change
the investigation.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
In live mode, GPT-5.6 is configured
to create these routes.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The learner chooses
the method.

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
They commit to
a first prediction.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Evidence stays locked
until they do.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
That preserves
a genuine before state.

13
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
The Evidence Lens separates evidence,
inference, and open questions.

14
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Aquarius supports up to six crew
with surface power, air, and data.

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,500
That does not prove a larger habitat
can be independent.

16
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:07,000
The learner writes
where the source stops.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,500
Then they mark how it changes
their original prediction.

18
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:16,000
One finding becomes
one design move.

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The exact anchor is
regular deliveries.

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
The creation repeats
regular deliveries.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
That visible phrase connects
design to creation.

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
It is a continuity check,
not grading.

23
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The learner names a tradeoff
and checks visible criteria.

24
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Then they finish
one focused design.

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,500
Reflection names what changed
and what remains uncertain.

26
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:49,000
The learner's words stay separate
from demo feedback.

27
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:53,500
The map makes that reasoning path
visible.

28
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:58,000
It keeps the learner's language
in view.

29
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,800
The learner selects
one next question.

30
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,600
The final card holds exact sources
and evidence judgment.

31
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:12,400
It also preserves the design move
and creation anchor.

32
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:17,200
The complete trace can be
copied and shared.

33
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:22,000
No grades, accounts,
or learner profiles.

34
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:27,000
In live mode, OpenAI web search
returns citations for evidence.

35
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
GPT-5.6 supports routes, quests,
evidence, and reflection.

36
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Its role is bounded;
learners decide.

37
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Codex made source boundaries
and evidence-to-design testable.

38
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Codex made the creation anchor
a visible continuity check.

39
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:54,000
ReasonWeave makes reasoning visible
and keeps humans responsible for it.
